{"name":"Vineyard View","hex":"#777146","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"vineyard","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A grape plantation, especially one used in the production of wine."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/vineyard"},{"term":"view","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Visual perception.\nThe act of seeing or looking at something.","The act of seeing or looking at something."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To look at.","To regard in a stated way."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/view"}],"entries":[{"title":"Vineyard","blocks":[{"text":"A vineyard is a plantation of grape-bearing vines. Many vineyards exist for winemaking; others for the production of raisins, table grapes, and non-alcoholic grape juice. The science, practice and study of vineyard production is known as viticulture. Vineyards are often characterised by their terroir, a French term loosely translating as \"a sense of place\" that refers to the specific geographical and geological characteristics of grapevine plantations, which may be imparted to the wine itself."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e5/Vineyards_in_Burgundy_France.jpg/330px-Vineyards_in_Burgundy_France.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vineyard"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/21/Vinepyrennees2.jpg/500px-Vinepyrennees2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/21/Vinepyrennees2.jpg/500px-Vinepyrennees2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The extensive vineyards of the Languedoc-Roussillon region, southern France","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AVinepyrennees2.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6b/Aerial_View_